{"name":"Endless River","hex":"#567aad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"endless","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having no end.","Extending indefinitely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/endless"},{"term":"river","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large and often winding stream which drains a land mass, carrying water down from higher areas to a lower point, oftentimes ending in another body of water, such as an ocean or in an inland sea.","Any large flow of a liquid in a single body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To improve one’s hand to beat another player on the final card in a poker game."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/river"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Endless River","blocks":[{"text":"The Endless River is the fifteenth and final studio album by the English rock band Pink Floyd, released in November 2014 by Parlophone Records in Europe and Columbia Records in the rest of the world. It was the third Pink Floyd album recorded under the leadership of the guitarist, David Gilmour, and the first following the death of the keyboardist and songwriter, Richard Wright, who appears posthumously. It was produced by Gilmour, Youth, Andy Jackson and Phil Manzanera."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/be/Pink_Floyd_-_The_Endless_River_%28Artwork%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Endless_River","wikidata":"Q17319538"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River","wikidata":"Q4022"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Rickwright.jpg/500px-Rickwright.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Rickwright.jpg/500px-Rickwright.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Endless River was created as a tribute to Pink Floyd founding member Rick Wright, who died in 2008.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARickwright.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/London%2C_The_O2%2C_The_Wall_Live%2C_2011-05-12_%2819%29_%286203136479%29.jpg/500px-London%2C_The_O2%2C_The_Wall_Live%2C_2011-05-12_%2819%29_%286203136479%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/London%2C_The_O2%2C_The_Wall_Live%2C_2011-05-12_%2819%29_%286203136479%29.jpg/1280px-London%2C_The_O2%2C_The_Wall_Live%2C_2011-05-12_%2819%29_%286203136479%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/London%2C_The_O2%2C_The_Wall_Live%2C_2011-05-12_%2819%29_%286203136479%29.jpg/500px-London%2C_The_O2%2C_The_Wall_Live%2C_2011-05-12_%2819%29_%286203136479%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Drummer Nick Mason (left) and 